PKI store and leaf certificates for expired CA/CRL validation unit tests (check_pki.c).

The store layout matches a standard S2OPC PKI directory. It contains every CA and CRL
required by the test scenarios (distinct CA subjects, one group per case). Leaf
certificates are kept outside trusted/ and supplied at validation time.

## Single-tier CA cases (Root → Leaf)

| Case | trusted/certs | trusted/crl | Certificate validated | Expected |
|------|---------------|-------------|----------------------|----------|
| 1 | ca_case1_valid.der | ca_case1_crl_valid.der | leaf_case1.der | Accepted |
| 2 | ca_case2_expired.der | ca_case2_crl_valid.der | leaf_case2.der | TimeInvalid |
| 3 | ca_case3_expired.der, ca_case3_valid.der | ca_case3_crl_valid.der | leaf_case3.der | Accepted |
| 4 | ca_case4_valid.der | ca_case4_crl_expired.der, ca_case4_crl_valid.der | leaf_case4.der | RevocationUnknown |
| 5 | ca_case5_valid.der | ca_case5_crl_expired_revoked.der, ca_case5_crl_valid.der | leaf_case5.der | RevocationUnknown |
| 6 | ca_selfsigned_expired.der | — | same self-signed cert | TimeInvalid |
| 7 | ca_case7_valid.der | ca_case7_crl_valid.der | leaf_expired_case7.der | TimeInvalid |

## Intermediate CA chains (Root → Intermediate → Leaf)

| Case | trusted/certs | trusted/crl | issuers/certs | issuers/crl | Certificate validated | Expected |
|------|---------------|-------------|---------------|-------------|----------------------|----------|
| int-1 | ca_int_case1_root.der, ca_int_case1_inter.der | ca_int_case1_root_crl.der, ca_int_case1_inter_crl.der | — | — | leaf_int_case1.der | Accepted |
| int-1b | ca_int_case1b_root.der | ca_int_case1b_root_crl.der | ca_int_case1b_inter.der | ca_int_case1b_inter_crl.der | leaf_int_case1b.der | Accepted |
| int-2 | ca_int_case2_root.der, ca_int_case2_inter.der (expired) | ca_int_case2_root_crl.der, ca_int_case2_inter_crl.der | — | — | leaf_int_case2.der | TimeInvalid |
| int-2b | ca_int_case2b_root.der (expired), ca_int_case2b_inter.der | ca_int_case2b_root_crl.der, ca_int_case2b_inter_crl.der | — | — | leaf_int_case2b.der | TimeInvalid |
| int-3 | ca_int_case3_root.der, ca_int_case3_inter_expired.der, ca_int_case3_inter_valid.der | ca_int_case3_root_crl.der, ca_int_case3_inter_crl.der | — | — | leaf_int_case3.der | Accepted |
| int-4 | ca_int_case4_root.der, ca_int_case4_inter.der | ca_int_case4_root_crl.der, ca_int_case4_inter_crl_expired.der, ca_int_case4_inter_crl_valid.der | — | — | leaf_int_case4.der | RevocationUnknown |
| int-4b | ca_int_case4b_root.der, ca_int_case4b_inter.der | ca_int_case4b_root_crl_expired.der, ca_int_case4b_root_crl_valid.der, ca_int_case4b_inter_crl.der | — | — | leaf_int_case4b.der | RevocationUnknown |

Regeneration (requires Python 3 and the `cryptography` package).
Certificate generation logic is shared via `../scripts/pki_gen/` (see `../scripts/README.md`).

```bash
cd tests/ClientServer/data/cert/expired_in_pki_test
python3 generate_certs.py
```

Do not commit private keys. DER files are committed so tests do not depend on generation at build time.

Tests load the full store with `SOPC_PKIProvider_CreateFromStore("./expired_in_pki_test")`.
